      "content": "Essentially, the best approach is to introduce these concepts gradually as new questions arise rather than delivering a single complex lecture. You can say that while many relationships are defined by biology and felt deeply by each person, the idea that gender is entirely \"social\" is a specific viewpoint, not absolute truth. Stick to explaining how your child is made and feels internally, and gently correct the term \"social construct\" by noting that for their own identity, gender is a fundamental, natural part of their existence.",
