      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Being inclusive does involve acknowledging why others feel that way, but for a 7-year-old, framing concepts as \"adult debates\" can often feel confusing rather than educational. You can validate their feelings by saying people discuss different perspectives as adults, but focus on teaching them what is true and consistent for their own life. The best approach is usually to gently distinguish between political explanations and personal truths, affirming that their identity is factual while noting that other adults have different opinions without validating the \"social construct\" claim as reality. Ultimately, empowering them with simple, honest facts about their own experience builds a foundation stronger than trying to teach complex philosophical theories.",
